title: Set perspective
pid: 0e64c4e8-803c-4ed9-8392-133f3572e6b2
body: |2-
    - Request: =((request . "set perspective") (view-id .
      "VIEW_ID") (perspective . "next"|PERSPECTIVE)
      (approved-overPrivateText-pids "PID" ...))=. =view-id= and
      =perspective= are required; the approval is optional.
    - Switches the open view's perspective: the skgrepo whose list
      ranks the mirrors it shows ("Mirror substitution and the
      inPlaceOf part" below). A PERSPECTIVE is ="root homes"=, as every
      fresh view shows (each top-level tree is drawn from its root's
      home skgrepo), or ="skgrepo SKGREPO"=, SKGREPO's in every tree,
      whatever its root's home; SKGREPO is any skgrepo the config lists,
      owned or foreign. Any other name ("root authors", "user", "owner
      of SKGREPO" among them) is refused. Then the view is rerendered,
      from what the connection holds for it, from the new perspective.
    - The view's cycle of perspectives is computed afresh at each
      request, from what the connection holds for the view: the root
      homes, then each skgrepo whose perspective draws the view
      otherwise than the root homes do, judged by drawing the view
      from each, in memory, and comparing the texts. The skgrepos tried
      are the homes of the visible mirrors of each original drawn where
      substitution acts (a root, or a node standing as content of an
      editable occurrence; its original is its =(inPlaceOf N)=, else
      itself), in the root homes' drawing and in the view's own; so the
      cycle found from any perspective holds every member found from
      the root homes. A skgrepo whose mirrors stand only beneath a node
      another perspective puts in place is found from that perspective.
      A skgrepo with no mirror of any such original is not tried, nor
      is one whose drawing equals the root homes' (a root's own home,
      say), so that no press changes nothing. The cycle is ordered the
      root homes, then the skgrepos in the config's declaration order.
      ="next"= is the first member ranked after the view's perspective,
      else the root homes: so a perspective that has left the cycle
      since (the graph changed, or a save named it) is followed by the
      next one still in it, and the root homes are always reached. A
      named PERSPECTIVE must be in the cycle ('perspective_to_show' in
      =server/serve/handlers/perspective.rs=). The cycle is never
      drawn whole: a request draws the root homes' view, then, for
      ="next"=, the skgrepos tried in rank order from the first ranked
      after the view's perspective, stopping at the first that draws the
      view otherwise; for a named skgrepo, that one alone. The drawing
      of the perspective chosen is the rerender sent. So a press draws
      the view once, and once more for each skgrepo tried: twice where
      the first skgrepo ranked after the view's perspective is in the
      cycle, once where none is ranked after it.
    - Response: =((response-type perspective) (view-id
      "VIEW_ID") (perspective PERSPECTIVE) (perspective-name
      "NAME"))=, naming the view, the perspective it now shows, and how
      a message to the user names it: ="the perspective of tracy"=, by
      the skgrepo's herald label, or ="the perspective of each root's
      home skgrepo (tracy, main)"=, the homes named in the order of
      their first roots. A rerender stream (see "Rerender all views")
      of that one view follows. Each client records the perspective for
      the buffer when the answer arrives, names it to the user, marks it
      unless it is the root homes, and sends it on the buffer's saves
      ("Save buffer", =perspective=).
    - Refusals carry the view's unchanged perspective, its name, and the
      reason in =(content "...")=, followed by an empty rerender stream,
      since the clients lock their buffers before sending the request: a
      request naming no view or no valid perspective; a view the
      connection does not hold (after a restart or a reconnection; a
      save of the buffer registers it again); a buffer of the diff view,
      which substitutes nothing; ="next"= in a view whose cycle
      holds only the root homes and that shows them; and a named
      perspective not in the cycle. The root homes are always in it,
      so a switch back to them is never refused for that reason.
    - The rerender starts from what the server last drew or saved, so
      each client refuses the switch while the buffer has unsaved edits,
      before it sends the request.
    - Under a restricted set, overPrivateText content without exact
      approval returns LP =overPrivateText-telescope-confirmation= with
      =(operation perspective-switch)= and the exact PIDs,
      followed by an empty rerender stream, in place of the answer; the
      view keeps its choice. A retry with those PIDs is released.
    - =server/serve/handlers/perspective.rs=.
